IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
-- EVERY-EACH-QUANTIFIER-SPEC §5.1.2 (R-X5 MODIFIED 2026-09-07, AMENDED
-- 2026-09-16; R-X6 RULED 2026-09-07; BUILT 2026-09-16): the window's two
-- edges. `WITHIN d [OF anchor]` was the closing edge (§5.1.1, run-anchors.l4);
-- this file adds the OPENING edge and the absolute forms:
--
--   AFTER d [OF anchor]     the window opens d after the anchor — or, with no
--                           anchor, d after the obligation's own clock
--   AFTER date              the window opens on that date
--   WITHIN d                beside an AFTER, counts from the instant the window
--                           OPENED (RE-ANCHOR, §5.1.2.2): AFTER 3 WITHIN 30 is
--                           [a+3, a+33]
--   WITHIN d OF THE JOIN    counts from the anchor named: AFTER 3 WITHIN 30 OF
--                           THE JOIN is the two-offset window [a+3, a+30]
--   BEFORE date             the window closes on that date
--
-- An act BEFORE the window opens is a NULLITY with a diagnostic (R-X6): it is
-- not performance and not a breach; the obligation stays live with its
-- deadline untouched; the run says so in a NOTE beside the result. Every
-- trace below pins one shape to the number it produces.

DECLARE Actor IS ONE OF
    Customer HAS name IS A STRING
    Shop     HAS name IS A STRING
    Landlord HAS name IS A STRING
    Tenant   HAS name IS A STRING

DECLARE Action IS ONE OF
    Deliver HAS who    IS AN Actor
    Order   HAS who    IS AN Actor
    Sign    HAS signer IS AN Actor
    Smoke   HAS who    IS AN Actor

buyer       MEANS Customer OF "Alice"
shop        MEANS Shop OF "Acme"
theLandlord MEANS Landlord OF "Ms Ng"
alice       MEANS Tenant OF "Alice"
bob         MEANS Tenant OF "Bob"
tenants     MEANS LIST alice, bob


§ `The cooling-off window: AFTER 3 WITHIN 30 re-anchors`

-- Meng's sentence: after the order is delivered, the customer may place a new
-- order after a three-day cooling-off period, within 30 days. Delivery at 10
-- opens the window at 13 and closes it at 43 — the WITHIN counts from the
-- instant the window opened, not from the delivery (§5.1.2.2). Written with
-- MUST so that a late act BREACHES and reports the deadline it missed.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`cooling off` MEANS
    PARTY shop MUST Deliver (EXACTLY shop) WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER 3 WITHIN 30
           HENCE FULFILLED)
    LEST BREACH

-- 12 is early: a nullity, reported. The residual is still live, printed as
-- the window it now is — AFTER 1 WITHIN 30 at instant 12 is [13, 43].
#TRACE `cooling off` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY shop DOES Deliver shop AT 10
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 12

-- 20 is in time
#TRACE `cooling off` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY shop DOES Deliver shop AT 10
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 20

-- 41 is in time: the window closes at 43, not at 40
#TRACE `cooling off` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY shop DOES Deliver shop AT 10
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 41

-- 43 is the last timely instant
#TRACE `cooling off` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY shop DOES Deliver shop AT 10
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 43

-- 44 is late: BREACH, reporting the deadline 43
#TRACE `cooling off` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY shop DOES Deliver shop AT 10
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 44

-- early, then in time: the early act did not consume the obligation
#TRACE `cooling off` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY shop DOES Deliver shop AT 10
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 12
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 20

-- The permission form of the same sentence. A MAY that is never exercised
-- in its window lapses to its LEST, which defaults to FULFILLED — so 44 is
-- not a breach here; it is a permission that expired unused.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`cooling off, may` MEANS
    PARTY shop MUST Deliver (EXACTLY shop) WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY buyer MAY Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER 3 WITHIN 30
           HENCE FULFILLED)
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `cooling off, may` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY shop DOES Deliver shop AT 10
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 12

#TRACE `cooling off, may` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY shop DOES Deliver shop AT 10
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 44


§ `The two-offset window: AFTER 3 WITHIN 30 OF THE JOIN`

-- Both edges from the delivery: [13, 40]. 40 is in time, 41 is late.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`two offset` MEANS
    PARTY shop MUST Deliver (EXACTLY shop) WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER 3 WITHIN 30 OF THE JOIN
           HENCE FULFILLED)
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `two offset` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY shop DOES Deliver shop AT 10
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 40

#TRACE `two offset` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY shop DOES Deliver shop AT 10
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 41

-- The AFTER may name its own anchor. With the WITHIN bare, it still
-- re-anchors from the instant the window opened: AFTER 3 OF THE JOIN
-- WITHIN 30 is [13, 43] — 43 in time, 44 late.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`after anchored` MEANS
    PARTY shop MUST Deliver (EXACTLY shop) WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER 3 OF THE JOIN WITHIN 30
           HENCE FULFILLED)
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `after anchored` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY shop DOES Deliver shop AT 10
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 43

#TRACE `after anchored` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY shop DOES Deliver shop AT 10
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 44

-- Both anchored to the join: [13, 40], the two-offset window again.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`both anchored` MEANS
    PARTY shop MUST Deliver (EXACTLY shop) WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER 3 OF THE JOIN WITHIN 30 OF THE JOIN
           HENCE FULFILLED)
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `both anchored` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY shop DOES Deliver shop AT 10
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 41

-- Two different anchors: opens 3 after the arming (0), closes 30 after the
-- join (10) — [3, 40]. 12 is in time.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`two origins` MEANS
    PARTY shop MUST Deliver (EXACTLY shop) WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER 3 OF THE ARMING WITHIN 30 OF THE JOIN
           HENCE FULFILLED)
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `two origins` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY shop DOES Deliver shop AT 10
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 12

-- A bare AFTER counts from the obligation's own clock — the join, under a
-- HENCE — whatever the WITHIN names. Beside WITHIN 2 OF THE DEADLINE it is
-- [join+3, deadline+2] = [13, 32]: two origins, and the window is open even
-- though 3 > 2. The checker compares a bare AFTER's literal offset only
-- against an anchor its clock can never precede (OF THE ARMING; OF THE JOIN
-- under HENCE; OF THE DEADLINE under a MUST's LEST), so this one checks and
-- runs: 20 and 32 in time, 33 late at 32. (The first cut refused it as
-- empty; adversarial pass of 2026-09-16, F1/R1-1.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`bare after, deadline within` MEANS
    PARTY shop MUST Deliver (EXACTLY shop) WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER 3 WITHIN 2 OF THE DEADLINE
           HENCE FULFILLED)
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `bare after, deadline within` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY shop DOES Deliver shop AT 10
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 20

#TRACE `bare after, deadline within` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY shop DOES Deliver shop AT 10
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 32

#TRACE `bare after, deadline within` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY shop DOES Deliver shop AT 10
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 33

-- The same with an instant as the anchor, at top level: the AFTER counts
-- from the arming (0), the WITHIN from the instant named — [30, 205]. An
-- instant bears no relation to the clock, so the checker never compares
-- against one: 100 in time, 206 late at 205.
closingDate MEANS 200

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`bare after, instant within` MEANS
    PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER 30 WITHIN 5 OF closingDate
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `bare after, instant within` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 100

#TRACE `bare after, instant within` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 206


§ `Under a LEST, the clock is the failure time`

-- The delivery is never made; its deadline is 30, and for a MUST the failure
-- time IS the missed deadline (§5.2). The cure window opens 3 after it and
-- runs 30 from where it opened: [33, 63]. 32 is early, 33 is in time — with
-- THE DEADLINE named, and with it left off: for a missed MUST the two
-- spellings coincide.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`cure from the deadline` MEANS
    PARTY shop MUST Deliver (EXACTLY shop) WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST (PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER 3 OF THE DEADLINE WITHIN 30
          HENCE FULFILLED)

#TRACE `cure from the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 32

#TRACE `cure from the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 33

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`cure, bare` MEANS
    PARTY shop MUST Deliver (EXACTLY shop) WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST (PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER 3 WITHIN 30
          HENCE FULFILLED)

#TRACE `cure, bare` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 63

#TRACE `cure, bare` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 64

-- For a SHANT the failure time is the VIOLATING act's stamp, not the end of
-- the prohibition's window (§5.2.1) — so there the two spellings differ.
-- Smoking at 5 violates a 30-day prohibition; the bare cure window counts
-- from 5: [8, 38] — 7 early, 38 in time, 39 late. THE DEADLINE names the
-- prohibition's end, 30: [33, 63] — 20 early, 33 in time. (The first cut's
-- doc page said the two coincide "with or without" the anchor; adversarial
-- pass of 2026-09-16, F2.)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`cure after violation, bare` MEANS
    PARTY buyer SHANT Smoke (EXACTLY buyer) WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST (PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER 3 WITHIN 30
          HENCE FULFILLED)

#TRACE `cure after violation, bare` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Smoke buyer AT 5
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 7

#TRACE `cure after violation, bare` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Smoke buyer AT 5
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 38

#TRACE `cure after violation, bare` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Smoke buyer AT 5
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 39

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`cure after violation, from the deadline` MEANS
    PARTY buyer SHANT Smoke (EXACTLY buyer) WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST (PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER 3 OF THE DEADLINE WITHIN 30
          HENCE FULFILLED)

#TRACE `cure after violation, from the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Smoke buyer AT 5
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 20

#TRACE `cure after violation, from the deadline` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Smoke buyer AT 5
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 33

-- So under a SHANT's LEST a bare AFTER beside WITHIN OF THE DEADLINE has two
-- origins — [violation+3, deadline+2] = [8, 32], open — and the checker does
-- not compare the literals. Under a MUST's LEST it does: the same literals
-- are refused in not-ok/tc/after-empty-window-lest.l4.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`cure after violation, deadline within` MEANS
    PARTY buyer SHANT Smoke (EXACTLY buyer) WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST (PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER 3 WITHIN 2 OF THE DEADLINE
          HENCE FULFILLED)

#TRACE `cure after violation, deadline within` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Smoke buyer AT 5
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 20


§ `Handed on as a value, the window is the machine's to judge`

-- The checker compares the literals of a bare AFTER beside WITHIN OF THE
-- DEADLINE only where the deonton IS the continuation it is written under.
-- A deonton that is an ARGUMENT to a function is a value: the function may
-- attach it under any obligation's LEST, and the anchors bind there, at
-- hand-off (§5.1.1). The same literal window, written under a MUST's LEST
-- both times, is handed once into a SHANT's LEST — where the failure time is
-- the smoking, and the window [11+3, 40+2] = [14, 42] is open — and once
-- into a MUST's, where it is [40+3, 40+2] and empty. The checker refuses
-- neither (it did refuse both until round 2 of the adversarial pass of
-- 2026-09-16, R2-1); the run reports the empty one.
GIVEN k IS A DEONTIC Actor Action
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`under a prohibition` k MEANS
    PARTY buyer SHANT Smoke (EXACTLY buyer) WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST k

GIVEN k IS A DEONTIC Actor Action
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`under an obligation` k MEANS
    PARTY buyer MUST Sign (EXACTLY buyer) WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST k

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`cure handed on, prohibition` MEANS
    PARTY shop MUST Deliver (EXACTLY shop) WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST (`under a prohibition` (PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER 3 WITHIN 2 OF THE DEADLINE
                                 HENCE FULFILLED
                                 LEST BREACH))

-- 13 is early, 20 and 42 in time, 43 late.
#TRACE `cure handed on, prohibition` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Smoke buyer AT 11
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 13

#TRACE `cure handed on, prohibition` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Smoke buyer AT 11
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 20

#TRACE `cure handed on, prohibition` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Smoke buyer AT 11
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 42

#TRACE `cure handed on, prohibition` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Smoke buyer AT 11
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 43

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`cure handed on, obligation` MEANS
    PARTY shop MUST Deliver (EXACTLY shop) WITHIN 10
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST (`under an obligation` (PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER 3 WITHIN 2 OF THE DEADLINE
                                 HENCE FULFILLED
                                 LEST BREACH))

-- The signature is never made; its deadline 40 passes; the order at 41
-- reveals that and is handed on to the cure, whose window is [43, 42]: the
-- run notes the empty window, and the early act's note says the window
-- closes before it opens rather than "once the window is open" (R2-4).
#TRACE `cure handed on, obligation` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 41

#TRACE `cure handed on, obligation` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 45


§ `AFTER alone: a right that vests and never expires`

-- The window opens at 13 and never closes. An act at 1000 is in time; an
-- act at 12 is early — and the note says the obligation has no closing edge,
-- there being no deadline to leave untouched; with no act at all the
-- residual prints as written.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`vests` MEANS
    PARTY shop MUST Deliver (EXACTLY shop) WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY buyer MAY Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER 3
           HENCE FULFILLED)
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `vests` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY shop DOES Deliver shop AT 10
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 1000

#TRACE `vests` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY shop DOES Deliver shop AT 10
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 12

#TRACE `vests` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY shop DOES Deliver shop AT 10


§ `The absolute forms: AFTER date, BEFORE date`

-- On a date-serial trace (the origin and every stamp a DATE_SERIAL), the
-- window opens 3 days after arming on 1 June and closes on 30 June. 3 June
-- is early, 4 June is in time, 30 June is the last timely day, 1 July is
-- late. The residual after the early act prints the remaining days, as an
-- anchored WITHIN's does.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`by june` MEANS
    PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER 3 BEFORE (YMD 2026 6 30)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `by june` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 3))

#TRACE `by june` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 4))

#TRACE `by june` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 30))

#TRACE `by june` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 7 1))

-- AFTER a date: the window opens on 10 June and runs 5 days from there.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`from june` MEANS
    PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER (YMD 2026 6 10) WITHIN 5
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `from june` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 9))

#TRACE `from june` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 15))

#TRACE `from june` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 16))

-- The same rules on a FLOATING trace (origin 0) are REFUSED, not silently
-- run against a serial in the 740,000s (§5.1.2.1, T1: nothing declares the
-- trace's scale; until it does, a date on a clock below DATE_SERIAL
-- (YMD 1 1 1) is refused by name). The refusal is a run-time error, not a
-- verdict.
#TRACE `by june` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 3

#TRACE `from june` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 3

-- The anchor form from run-anchors.l4, `WITHIN 0 OF (YMD …)`, is refused on
-- the same floating trace for the same reason — it was silently FULFILLED
-- before 2026-09-16 — and still runs on a date-serial one.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`anchored to june` MEANS
    PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) WITHIN 0 OF (YMD 2026 6 30)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `anchored to june` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 3

#TRACE `anchored to june` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 3))


§ `A barrier's HENCE with an opening edge`

-- The join fires at the last signature, 8; the landlord's window is
-- [11, 41]. 10 is early, 41 in time, 42 late.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`barrier then window` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants MUST Sign (EXACTLY t) WITHIN 30
      ONCE ALL HAVE
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) AFTER 3 WITHIN 30
           HENCE FULFILLED)
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `barrier then window` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 5
  PARTY bob DOES Sign bob AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 10

#TRACE `barrier then window` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 5
  PARTY bob DOES Sign bob AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 41

#TRACE `barrier then window` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 5
  PARTY bob DOES Sign bob AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 42

-- The members' own act may carry the window too: each tenant's [3, 33]
-- from the EVERY's arming. Alice's signature at 2 is early and reported;
-- Bob's at 4 is in time; Alice's residual at 4 has 29 to run.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`barrier window` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants MUST Sign (EXACTLY t) AFTER 3 WITHIN 30
      ONCE ALL HAVE
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `barrier window` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 2
  PARTY bob DOES Sign bob AT 4

#TRACE `barrier window` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 2
  PARTY bob DOES Sign bob AT 4
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 5


§ `A fork with an opening edge`

-- Each member's window is [3, 33]. Alice's early signature at 2 is a
-- nullity; her second at 4 counts; Bob's at 33 is timely.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`fork window` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants MUST Sign (EXACTLY t) AFTER 3 WITHIN 30
      UPON EACH
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `fork window` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 2
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 4
  PARTY bob DOES Sign bob AT 33

-- Alice never signs again: at 33, her obligation has 0 to run and the
-- window's opening is spent, so the residual prints as a plain WITHIN 0.
#TRACE `fork window` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 2
  PARTY bob DOES Sign bob AT 33


-- A join-line WITHIN bounds the whole from the EVERY's arming (R-T2) and is
-- not re-anchored by a member's AFTER: with AFTER 3 on the act and WITHIN 30
-- on the join line, each member's window is [3, 30] — the demoted deadline
-- is handed to the member as WITHIN 30 OF THE ARMING, and the note reports
-- the window closing at 30, not 33. Alice at 2 is early, Bob at 30 is
-- timely, Alice at 31 is late.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`fork bounded as a whole` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants MUST Sign (EXACTLY t) AFTER 3
      UPON EACH WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `fork bounded as a whole` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 2
  PARTY bob DOES Sign bob AT 30

#TRACE `fork bounded as a whole` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 2
  PARTY bob DOES Sign bob AT 30
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 31


§ `A SHANT with an opening edge: the early act is not a violation`

-- No smoking from 3 to 33. Smoking at 2 is before the prohibition starts:
-- not a violation, not performance — a nullity, reported; the prohibition
-- stays in force. Smoking at 5 is the violation. Smoking at 2 and then at
-- 40, after the window closed, is a kept prohibition: FULFILLED.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`no smoking later` MEANS
    PARTY buyer SHANT Smoke (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER 3 WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `no smoking later` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Smoke buyer AT 2

#TRACE `no smoking later` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Smoke buyer AT 5

#TRACE `no smoking later` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Smoke buyer AT 2
  PARTY buyer DOES Smoke buyer AT 40


§ `The empty window a run reveals`

-- With literal offsets, AFTER 30 WITHIN 5 OF THE JOIN is a check error
-- (not-ok/tc/after-empty-window.l4). With the offsets as parameters the
-- checker cannot see it, and the run reports it: the window [38, 13] closes
-- before it opens. Every act is early or late; here the delivery at 20 is
-- late (the deadline was 13) and the one at 10 is early.
GIVEN d1 IS A NUMBER
      d2 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`window of` d1 d2 MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) AFTER d1 WITHIN d2 OF THE JOIN
           HENCE FULFILLED)
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `window of` 30 5 AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 20

#TRACE `window of` 30 5 AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 10

-- The same parameters with a bare WITHIN cannot be empty: [38, 43].
GIVEN d1 IS A NUMBER
      d2 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`window of, bare` d1 d2 MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) AFTER d1 WITHIN d2
           HENCE FULFILLED)
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `window of, bare` 30 5 AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 43

-- The note is worded per the shape it met (the first cut said "both edges
-- count from one anchor … drop the anchor from the WITHIN" for every shape;
-- adversarial pass of 2026-09-16, F3). A bare AFTER beside a WITHIN anchored
-- to the arming: the AFTER counts from the join (8), the WITHIN from the
-- arming (0) — [38, 5].
GIVEN d1 IS A NUMBER
      d2 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`window of, arming` d1 d2 MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) AFTER d1 WITHIN d2 OF THE ARMING
           HENCE FULFILLED)
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `window of, arming` 30 5 AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 20

-- Two anchors: the AFTER from the join, the WITHIN from the arming — [38, 5].
GIVEN d1 IS A NUMBER
      d2 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`window of, two anchors` d1 d2 MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord MUST Deliver (EXACTLY theLandlord) AFTER d1 OF THE JOIN WITHIN d2 OF THE ARMING
           HENCE FULFILLED)
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `window of, two anchors` 30 5 AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Deliver theLandlord AT 20

-- A BEFORE date earlier than the opening: opens 40 days after 1 June, on
-- 11 July; closes on 10 June. No anchor anywhere for the note to talk about.
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`window before` d MEANS
    PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER d BEFORE (YMD 2026 6 10)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `window before` 40 AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 20))

-- An AFTER date beside an anchored WITHIN: opens on 10 June, closes 5 days
-- after the arming on 1 June. The checker compares literal OFFSETS only, so
-- a date opening is never a check error; the note says the date is later
-- than where the WITHIN closes — not that both edges count from the arming,
-- which a date does not (adversarial pass of 2026-09-16, round 2, R2-3).
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`window from june` MEANS
    PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER (YMD 2026 6 10) WITHIN 5 OF THE ARMING
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `window from june` AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 1)) WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT (DATE_SERIAL (YMD 2026 6 20))

-- A SHANT whose window is empty: the early smoking is not a violation, and
-- the note says the prohibition ends before its window opens, so nothing can
-- violate it — not that it "stays in force" until a window that never opens.
GIVEN d1 IS A NUMBER
      d2 IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`window of, shant` d1 d2 MEANS
    PARTY alice MUST Sign (EXACTLY alice) WITHIN 30
    HENCE (PARTY theLandlord SHANT Smoke (EXACTLY theLandlord) AFTER d1 WITHIN d2 OF THE JOIN
           HENCE FULFILLED)
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `window of, shant` 30 5 AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 8
  PARTY theLandlord DOES Smoke theLandlord AT 10

-- A member's AFTER later than the join line's WITHIN: the demoted join-line
-- deadline reaches each member anchored OF THE ARMING by the machine's own
-- hand (`fork bounded as a whole` above), and the note says the WITHIN
-- counts from the arming — not "drop the anchor", which the drafter never
-- wrote. Each member's window is [40, 30]. The window's note is reported
-- ONCE, not once per member — a note is said once per directive — while
-- each early act is its own note, naming its party and stamp.
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`fork bounded, empty` MEANS
    EVERY Tenant t IN tenants MUST Sign (EXACTLY t) AFTER 40
      UPON EACH WITHIN 30
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH

#TRACE `fork bounded, empty` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY alice DOES Sign alice AT 2
  PARTY bob DOES Sign bob AT 4

-- A LEST chain that re-arms the same empty window until the stall guard
-- refuses it (run-lest.l4, §5.2.1) reports the window's note ONCE beside the
-- refusal, not once per hand-off (the first cut printed it 1001 times;
-- adversarial pass of 2026-09-16, F4).
GIVEN d IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
retry d MEANS
    PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER d WITHIN 0 OF 2
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST (retry d)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Actor Action
`stalled window` MEANS
    PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) WITHIN 2
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST (retry 3)

#TRACE `stalled window` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY buyer DOES Order buyer AT 100


§ `The printers`

-- An obligation evaluated without a trace prints back in its source form,
-- keyword by keyword, and the natural-language annotation reads the window
-- aloud: bare, a WITHIN beside an AFTER is "within 30 of that".
#EVAL PARTY buyer MAY Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER 3 WITHIN 30
#EVAL PARTY buyer MAY Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER 3 OF THE ARMING WITHIN 30 OF THE ARMING
#EVAL PARTY buyer MUST Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER 3 BEFORE (YMD 2026 6 30)
#EVAL PARTY buyer MAY Order (EXACTLY buyer) AFTER (YMD 2026 6 10)
